---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import CalculatorCard from "../components/CalculatorCard.astro";
import { calculators } from "../data/calculators.js";

const travelCalculators = calculators.filter(
  (calculator) => calculator.category === "Travel"
);
---

<Layout title="Travel Budget Calculators | ShouldISpend">
  <style>
    .container {
      max-width: 1100px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 80px 24px;
    }

    .eyebrow {
      color: var(--accent);
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 2px;
      font-size: 0.8rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      margin-bottom: 16px;
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: 4rem;
      line-height: 1;
      margin-bottom: 24px;
      max-width: 850px;
    }

    .intro {
      max-width: 760px;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      line-height: 1.8;
      margin-bottom: 56px;
    }

    .grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr));
      gap: 24px;
      margin-top: 32px;
    }

    .content-section {
      max-width: 760px;
      margin-top: 80px;
    }

    .content-section h2 {
      font-size: 2rem;
      margin-bottom: 20px;
    }

    .content-section p {
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.8;
      margin-bottom: 18px;
    }
  </style>

  <main class="container">
    <div class="eyebrow">Travel Calculators</div>

    <h1>Travel Budget Calculators and Vacation Affordability Tools</h1>

    <p class="intro">
      Travel spending can feel worth it emotionally while still creating financial pressure afterward. These calculators help you evaluate whether vacations, trips, flights, hotels, and family travel plans fit your savings, debt load, income, and long-term flexibility.
    </p>

    <div class="grid">
      {travelCalculators.map((calculator) => (
        <CalculatorCard
          category={calculator.category}
          title={calculator.title}
          description={calculator.description}
          href={calculator.href}
        />
      ))}
    </div>

    <section class="content-section">
  <h2>How Much Should You Spend on Travel?</h2>

  <p>
    A travel budget should be judged by more than the trip price. Savings cushion,
    debt, emergency needs, upcoming bills, and how quickly you can recover after
    the trip all matter.
  </p>

  <p>
    A trip that fits comfortably should create memories without creating months
    of financial stress afterward. The best travel budget leaves room for the
    experience, the return home, and the next financial priority.
  </p>

  <h2>Compare Different Types of Travel Spending</h2>

  <p>
    A Disney vacation, honeymoon, Europe trip, weekend getaway, and family vacation
    can all create different kinds of financial pressure. The right question is not
    just whether the trip sounds worth it. The real question is whether the cost
    still fits after savings, debt, income, and normal monthly obligations are
    considered.
  </p>

  <p>
    ShouldISpend travel calculators are designed to give a plain-English verdict
    instead of a generic budget rule. Use them to compare trip types, adjust the
    cost, and decide whether to book now, reduce the budget, or wait.
  </p>
</section>
  </main>
</Layout>